! X35 interim polar (Expedition format: TWS  TWA BSP  TWA BSP ...; knots and degrees)
! Source: ORC certificate "X-35 ONE DESIGN" (class X-35 OD, designer Jeppesen, builder X-Yachts),
!         VPP 2019 1.01, https://data.orc.org/public/od/2019/x35.od.pdf
!         (c) Offshore Racing Congress 2019. Derived numbers, used with attribution.
! Derivation: the 52-150 deg rows are the certificate boat speeds verbatim; the first point of each
!         line is the certificate beat angle with BSP = beat VMG / cos(beat angle), the run point is
!         the gybe angle with BSP = run VMG / -cos(gybe angle).
! INTERIM: this is the generic X35 polar used until the owner's own X35 polar file is loaded
!         (drop polar.json into the race pack). VPP numbers are optimistic for night racing with a
!         short-handed crew: the efficiency setting (default 0.92) scales every target speed.
